      "inputTokens": 86,
      "outputTokens": 607,
      "costUsd": 0.005506,
      "pronunciationText": "Here's a first car loan. You borrow thirty thousand dollars for a used car, and each month interest of zero point six per cent is added, so the balance is multiplied by one point zero zero six. Then your six hundred dollar repayment comes off. So what do you owe now? And next month, will more of your six hundred dollars go towards the debt, less, or the same? Make a guess."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-02",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-f09/scene-02.wav",
      "durationInFrames": 1050,
      "worstWordGap": {
        "seconds": 0.8219999999999876,
        "after": "owe.",
        "before": "In"
      },
      "cues": [
        {
          "text": "dollars",
          "start": 34.29800000000001,
          "end": 34.56137500000001
        }
      ],
      "seconds": 35,
      "peakFraction": 0.834014892578125,
      "fullScaleSamples": 0,
      "silencesAtLeast1_5s": [],
      "lowScoreWords": [
        {
          "word": "is",
          "start": 18.41599999999999,
          "end": 18.51599999999999,
          "score": 0.426
        },
        {
          "word": "the",
          "start": 29.273000000000014,
          "end": 29.334000000000014,
          "score": 0
        }
      ],
      "successfulRequestCount": 1,
      "loggedRequestAttempts": 1,
      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 119,
      "outputTokens": 875,
      "costUsd": 0.0079345,
      "pronunciationText": "The principal is the amount you borrow, and the balance is the amount you still owe. In a reducing-balance loan, interest is charged on the balance you still owe, not on the amount you first borrowed. The rate is seven point two per cent a year, compounded monthly, so each month's rate r is seven point two over twelve, which is zero point six per cent. Each month, first the interest is added, so the balance is multiplied by one plus r. Then the repayment comes off. So you now owe twenty-nine thousand five hundred and eighty dollars."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-03",
      "changed": true,
      "audio": "public/audio/math-a12-f09/scene-03.wav",
