      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 115,
      "outputTokens": 883,
      "costUsd": 0.0080045,
      "pronunciationText": "That one month is the whole rule. Call the balance after n months A sub n, so A zero is the thirty thousand you borrowed. A rule that gives the next value from the one before is called a recurrence. Here, A sub n plus one equals one plus r, times ay sub n, minus M, the repayment. Without the repayment, this would just be compound interest. So a reducing-balance loan is a compound interest loan with a repayment taken off every period. And interest comes first, because the repayment is made at the end of the month."
    },
