      "inputTokens": 139,
      "outputTokens": 860,
      "costUsd": 0.0078095000000000005,
      "pronunciationText": "Here are three months in a table. Each row's interest is zero point six per cent of what's owed at the start. In month one, that's one hundred and eighty dollars, so the repayment pays off four hundred and twenty dollars of the debt. In month two, the balance is lower, so the interest is one hundred and seventy-seven dollars forty-eight, leaving four hundred and twenty-two dollars fifty-two for the debt. In month three, the interest is one hundred and seventy-four dollars ninety-four, rounded to the cent, and the balance falls to twenty-eight thousand, seven hundred and thirty-two dollars forty-two."
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-05",
      "changed": true,
