      "possibleRetry": false,
      "inputTokens": 115,
      "outputTokens": 834,
      "costUsd": 0.0075635,
      "pronunciationText": "Now find the pattern behind the table. A one is thirty thousand times one point zero zero six, minus six hundred. For A two, multiply all of that by one point zero zero six, then take off another six hundred. That's thirty thousand times one point zero zero six squared, minus six hundred times one point zero zero six, minus six hundred. In A three, the loan has grown for three months. The first repayment has been off the balance for two months, so it has stopped two months of interest. The last has stopped none at all."
    },
