      "pronunciationText": "In general, A sub n equals P times one plus r to the n, minus M times one plus r to the n, minus one, all over r. Read it as two pieces. The first is what the loan would grow to with compound interest and no repayments. The second is the repayments, each grown by interest from the month it was paid, because paying it stopped that much debt from growing. What you owe is the difference. For three months it gives twenty-eight thousand, seven hundred and thirty-two dollars forty-two, the same as the table."
