      "costUsd": 0.005712,
      "pronunciationText": "Now zoom out to a home loan: four hundred thousand dollars at five per cent a year, compounded monthly, repaid over thirty years at two thousand one hundred and forty-seven dollars twenty-nine a month. In the first month, more than three quarters of the repayment is interest. So the balance falls slowly at first, then faster and faster. You don't owe less than half until about twenty years."
